  "question": {
    "text": "The plane $2 x-y+z=4$ intersects the line segment joining the points $\\mathrm{A}(\\mathrm{a},-2,4)$ and $\\mathrm{B}(2, \\mathrm{~b},-3)$ at the point $\\mathrm{C}$ in the ratio $2: 1$ and the distance of the point $\\mathrm{C}$ from the origin is $\\sqrt{5}$. If $a b&lt;0$ and $\\mathrm{P}$ is the point $(\\mathrm{a}-\\mathrm{b}, \\mathrm{b}, 2 \\mathrm{~b}-\\mathrm{a})$ then $\\mathrm{CP}^2$ is equal to:",
    "image": null
